Third-party components
----------------------

Only the V-JEPA 2 code below is vendored in this repository. The other components are
downloaded at install or run time. Each remains under its own licence. Weights or files
derived from them that Inferensys redistributes are listed with the release that
contains them.

V-JEPA 2 code
  https://github.com/facebookresearch/vjepa2 at commit
  204698b45b3712590f06245fbfba32d3be539812. MIT License, Copyright (c) Meta Platforms,
  Inc. and affiliates. The V-JEPA 2.1 ViT-B encoder definition (vit_base and the modules
  it uses, from app/vjepa_2_1/models/ and two helpers from src/) is vendored in
  bulwark/model/vjepa21, trimmed to what the encoder needs, with Meta's copyright
  headers and the MIT licence text (bulwark/model/vjepa21/LICENSE); each file's header
  says what changed. scripts/fetch_pretrained.sh also clones the repository at that
  commit into third_party/vjepa2, which only the test comparing the vendored code with
  Meta's uses. Three files in that repository (src/datasets/utils/video/randaugment.py,
  src/datasets/utils/video/randerase.py, src/datasets/utils/worker_init_fn.py) are under
  the Apache License 2.0; none of them is vendored.

V-JEPA 2.1 ViT-B/16 checkpoint
  https://dl.fbaipublicfiles.com/vjepa2/vjepa2_1_vitb_dist_vitG_384.pt, published by
  Meta in the V-JEPA 2 repository, whose licence is the MIT License, Copyright (c) Meta
  Platforms, Inc. and affiliates; the repository states no separate licence for its
  checkpoints. Bulwark-B1 training checkpoints contain the LoRA adapters and heads trained
  by Bulwark and the encoder's final output norm, fine-tuned from this checkpoint; they
  do not contain the rest of the encoder, which users download themselves. A Bulwark-B1
  release written by bulwark release (bulwark.inference.save_release,
  examples/make_release.py) contains the full encoder weights, derived from this
  checkpoint with the LoRA adapters merged in, and ships the MIT licence text with
  Meta's copyright notice as LICENSE-vjepa2.

timm and EfficientViT-B1 weights
  timm (https://github.com/huggingface/pytorch-image-models), Apache License 2.0.
  Bulwark-E1 is initialised from timm's efficientvit_b1.r224_in1k weights, Apache
  License 2.0 per the model card (https://huggingface.co/timm/efficientvit_b1.r224_in1k),
  trained on ImageNet-1k. EfficientViT (https://github.com/mit-han-lab/efficientvit) is
  by MIT Han Lab, Apache License 2.0. Redistributed Bulwark-E1 weights are modified from
  these weights: Inferensys trained them further on Bulwark's training data, with
  distillation from Bulwark-B1.

MediaPipe Face Landmarker (teacher model, optional)
  https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-models/face_landmarker/face_landmarker/float16/1/face_landmarker.task,
  Google. The model cards of its Face Mesh V2 and Blendshape V2 components state the
  Apache License 2.0. Used only to produce training labels.

RF-DETR (teacher model, optional)
  https://github.com/roboflow/rf-detr, Roboflow. The rfdetr package and the Nano,
  Small and Medium detection models used here are under the Apache License 2.0. Used
  only to produce training labels.

Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct (teacher model, optional)
  https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct, Qwen team, Apache License 2.0 per
  its model card, run through the MLX conversion
  https://huggingface.co/mlx-community/Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct-4bit (Apache License 2.0
  per its model card). Used only to produce training labels.

Wan2.2-TI2V-5B (synthetic data generator, optional)
  https://huggingface.co/Wan-AI/Wan2.2-TI2V-5B, Apache License 2.0. Its model card
